content.main_review:
Pros:
1.	The paper is well written and the intuition is demonstrated well;
2.	The experiments are conducted in four benchmark datasets, which validates the proposed approach sufficiently;
3.	The causal perspective in meta-learning opens a new door to improving meta-learning.

Cons:
1.	The description of the proposed algorithm is not clear in the main body. I suggest that the pseudo-codes in the appendix is placed to the Section 3;
2.	Although the intuition of proposed approaches is clear and demonstrated well, the improvements are incremental in contrast to MetaMix, which weakens its effectiveness;
3.	Please indicate the reference of claims “In meta-learning, there are two types of overfitting problems:” In section 2.1.
